Z||000008||rogergarrison||09-17-2001||12:13 PM||||those were put on by previous owners. They say some differnt things and just stick on the oem handles.<P>in factory Special Editions, it usually applies to a special options package, like leather interior, or exterior trim. Also a lot of factory SE is just the label they put on cars assembled out of the previous years left over parts. Like you could have a new 2001 Honda thats got new 2000 suspension or brake parts. My Mercedes was built with the previous years brakes, which were a completely different set up, but it was still a new car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bigred||09-17-2001||07:09 PM||||I have a 1987 gt with the same tag on the door handle, nothing about the car is unusual. I would like to place something else in there but don't know what.  They semm to have been hot glued on.||||reg||1
Z||000010||flyntus||09-17-2001||08:17 PM||||Those "Special Edition" tags were bought at Auto accessory store, i.e. Pep Boys, Advance, etc.  I have a set that are similar except mine says "Pontiac". I got them back in 1985/86.  They have a self-adhesive strip & you just stick them on.  Mine has stayed on since 85/86.<BR>||||reg||12
